      "id": "be4ex6c",
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 2,
      "content": "1. Background of the Maratha Power"
    },
    {
      "type": "keyFacts",
      "title": "Key Takeaways",
      "items": [
        "Shivaji Maharaj laid the foundation of the Maratha Empire in western India in the 17th century.",
        "The administration was run with the help of an eight-minister council known as the Ashta Pradhan.",
        "The military relied heavily on guerrilla warfare tactics known as Ganimi Kava and maintained a permanent navy.",
        "Revenue was bolstered through taxes like Chauth (one-fourth of land revenue) and Sardeshmukhi (an additional 10%).",
        "The empire reached its territorial peak during the Peshwa era before facing decline after the Third Battle of Panipat."
      ],
      "id": "fn9s9p2"
    },
